{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784648156,"nonce":"73jSjlkxQ7CifoKAzbVMJIzXtdE=","message":"## Root-cause analysis\n\nb4 recognises a bracketed annotation between trailers only when it is a\n**single line**. Luigi's annotation spans two lines, so neither line is\nrecognised as trailer-adjacent, both are reclassified as body text, and the\nmessage-rebuild step always emits body *above* the trailer block — moving\nthe annotation out of the sign-off chain.\n\n**Trailer parsing** — `LoreMessage.find_trailers()`, `src/b4/__init__.py`:\n\n1. A trailer line must match `^\\s*(\\w\\S+):\\s+(\\S.*)` (line 2785) — i.e.\n   `Key: value`. `[LL: something` does not match, so it is not a trailer.\n2. The one accommodation for annotations is the \"extended info\" branch\n   (lines 2842-2846):\n\n        if len(line) \u003e 2 and was_trailer and re.search(r'^\\s*\\[[^]]+]\\s*$', line):\n            trailers[-1].extinfo = line\n\n   This requires the annotation to be a **complete `[...]` on one line** and\n   to immediately follow a trailer (`was_trailer`). For the two-line input:\n\n        Signed-off-by: Paolo Abeni \u003cpabeni@redhat.com\u003e\n        [LL: something\n        something]\n        Signed-off-by: Luigi Leonardi \u003cleonardi@redhat.com\u003e\n\n   line 2 (`[LL: something`) has no closing `]` → fails the regex; the code\n   sets `was_trailer = False` and appends it to `others`. Line 3\n   (`something]`) also fails and joins `others`. So the annotation lands in\n   the non-trailer bucket.\n\n**Reconstruction hoists body above trailers** — `get_body_parts()` returns\nthose `others` as body text, and `rebuild_message()` (`__init__.py:~2869`)\nplus `fix_trailers()` (`__init__.py:~3122`) always write\n`body` → blank line → trailer block. The annotation, now body, is therefore\nemitted before both Signed-off-by lines — exactly result [2] the reporter\nsaw. A single-line `[LL: …]` would have been captured as `extinfo` and\npreserved in place; the multi-line form is what breaks.\n\n**No opt-out.** The only related config is trailer *ordering*\n(`trailer-order` / `send-trailer-order`, `__init__.py:~3034` /\n`ez.py:~3924`); neither disables the body/trailer reclassification, and\nthere is no flag to preserve interspersed non-trailer lines. The move also\nhappens silently — no warning at send time.\n\n## Related bugs\n\nSame trailer-parsing engine as `e1ed6cb` and `ddb36e5` (all `trailers`),\nthough a distinct failure: this is line-classification/reconstruction, not\ncross-revision collection. No fix suggestions per request.","files":null}]}